<comment datatype='string'>During the degradation of &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD-19011&quot;&gt;methyl &lt;i&gt;tert&lt;/i&gt;-butyl ether&lt;/a&gt; (MTBE) the intermediate &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=ACETOACETYL-COA&quot;&gt;acetoacetyl-CoA&lt;/a&gt; is potentially converted by &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?type=EC-NUMBER&amp;object=EC-2.3.1.9&quot;&gt;EC 2.3.1.9, acetyl-CoA &lt;em&gt;C&lt;/em&gt;-acetyltransferase&lt;/a&gt;, to two acetyl-CoA molecules that can feed into the tricarboxylic acid cycle.
&lt;p&gt;
The &lt;a href=&quot;/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=G-44561&quot;&gt;Mpe_A3367&lt;/a&gt; gene of &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-420662&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Methylibium petroleiphilum&lt;/i&gt; PM1&lt;/a&gt;, which is located on the chromosome, is predicted to encode acetyl-CoA acetyltransferase [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/17158667&quot;&gt;Kane07&lt;/a&gt;]. The gene is 1.6-fold upregulated by exposure to &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD-19011&quot;&gt;methyl &lt;i&gt;tert&lt;/i&gt;-butyl ether&lt;/a&gt; (MTBE), and thus was proposed to catalyze this predicted activity during MTBE degradation [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/17158667&quot;&gt;Kane07&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/17890343&quot;&gt;Hristova07&lt;/a&gt;].
</comment>
